{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Garmin Connect Personal API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "summary": "Read-only pull access to one's own Garmin Connect data.",
    "description": "Reconstructed, not official. Paths and operation summaries come from the Personal API Swagger page as saved on 2026-10-23; parameters, the base URL and the token exchange come from Garmin's own Python client (github.com/garmin/connect-personal-api-python, Apache-2.0).\n\nWhat is deliberately absent: request and response schemas. The saved page listed the model *names* only - it was saved with every model collapsed, so no property was ever in the page - and inventing them would produce a document that looks authoritative and is wrong. The names are kept under `x-garmin-schema-names` so nothing is lost.\n\nVerify against the live Swagger docs before relying on it."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://personal.connectapi.garmin.com"
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "bearerAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "components": {
    "securitySchemes": {
      "bearerAuth": {
        "type": "http",
        "scheme": "bearer",
        "bearerFormat": "JWT",
        "description": "The token from the token endpoint. Valid up to 24 hours, no refresh token."
      },
      "personalApiKey": {
        "type": "apiKey",
        "in": "header",
        "name": "Authorization",
        "description": "The personal API key, as `ApiKey <key>`. Created in Garmin Connect on the web under Settings, and valid for 30, 90 or 180 days or one year."
      }
    }
  },
